NetUSBee/EtherNEC driver for FreeMiNT

An NE2000 compatible card on the cartridge port: the Ethernet part of the
NetUSBee (an RTL8019AS) or an ISA card in an EtherNEC adapter. The card
must be configured for I/O address 0x300, which is how the NetUSBee comes.

The driver is a port of the Linux ne driver and 8390 core
(drivers/net/ethernet/8390/ne.c, lib8390.c and 8390.h) with the cartridge
port ISA emulation of arch/m68k/include/asm/raw_io.h. Names are kept as in
Linux so that fixes can be carried over. See the comments at the top of
ne.c for what was left out.

The card has no interrupt line. It is polled from the 200 Hz system timer,
which is where the EtherNE driver polls it from and what Linux does from
an MFP timer. The MAC address comes from the card's PROM; it can be
replaced while the interface is down with

	ifconfig en0 hwaddr 00:20:43:58:78:3c

Installation

Copy netusbee.xif to the MiNT directory. The 000 build is for the 68000,
the 02060 build for the 68020 and up; the latter adds a nop after every
write to the cartridge port, which the EtherNE driver found the faster
machines need.

The USB part of the NetUSBee is handled by the driver in
sys/usb/src.km/ucd/netusbee.
